                <pb facs="0315" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60p2/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Coleman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-02T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1928—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Your 3, January 10, 1 p.m. Transit Article. This Government would agree to
                    insertion of following sentence after first sentence of first paragraph of
                    Article 16: “However the measures which either of the High Contracting Parties
                    may be obliged to take in case of emergency affecting the safety or vital
                    interests of the State may, in exceptional cases and for as short a period as
                    possible, involve a deviation from the provisions of this paragraph, it being
                    understood, however, that the principle of freedom of transit must be observed
                    to the utmost possible extent.” Make a separate paragraph of sentence beginning
                    with “Persons and goods”, and ending with “other matter”. Article 16 will then
                    have four paragraphs. For your information (1) it is understood that the
                    exception herein agreed to does not have reference to charges but only to
                    temporary interruptions of transit. (2) The Department considers that this idea
                    is better conveyed by Article 16 as herein amended than by the Latvian
                    proposal.</p>
                <p>The question of an exception in regard to State monopolies will be made the
                    subject of a separate telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
